WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.020
Film Courage: John we’ve known you for I
think ten years?

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.020
John Paul Rice, Producer: Yes.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:07.600
Film Courage: Okay a long time and I know
you’ve come up with some great analogies

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.809
which I would love to go into later.

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:12.879
I know you talk about the Red Carpet Producer
which I still love that term…anyway.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:17.430
But one thing I want to ask you about and
I heard you say it somewhere else you said

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:22.260
“Being in Hollywood and staying here for
a length of time will not maybe change you

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.779
but it will just make you more of what you
already are.”

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:25.810
Is that right?

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.810
John: Yes.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:31.429
That was the advice that was given to me any
years ago before I moved out here by a person

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:38.160
who worked in Hollywood with Jerry Bruckheimer
and he said “John you want to take a really

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.660
good stock of yourself…here…now because
everything that you do here, because everything

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.740
that you think, everything that you believe,
everything that you indulge in (good or bad)

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:54.020
it will be available to you out here at a
much greater level and degree and things you

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.020
don’t even know about are abundant.”

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.550
And he said “You will become more of who
you are.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.510
Rather than it changing you, you’ll actually
be able to fulfill all of those things that

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:12.760
are both inside of you and how you feel and
how you see the world and the kind of friends

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.760
that you hang out with and things you go and
do in your spare time."

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.430
And so I took that to heart.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:25.680
I didn’t understand it other than in the
observable “Okay, he’s telling me to think

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.560
about myself and to think about who I am deeply.”

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:39.350
I wasn’t worried in that regard but in my
18 years out here I would say that that statement

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.850
is still very true today.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.970
Not just for myself but for any of us.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:51.390
I think it’s…Hollywood affords you a lot
of things (not just the film industry) but

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.380
Los Angeles it’s abundant.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.190
It’s abundant everywhere you want to go.

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:59.870
There are several Starbucks within walking
distance, there are multiple places and things

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:05.250
that you can do and there’s also a variety
of people that maybe in your small town there

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:12.860
were only one or two there are now dozens
if not hundreds and a lot of them have money.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:22.640
And taking that into perspective and looking
at these last several years of growth, it

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.670
can challenge you, too.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:31.120
The only answer that I have for that is really
to look deeper within yourself and some of

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.530
those things that you have to look deeper
within can be painful.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:42.590
They can cause you to feel disappointed about
when you don’t get what you want, that when

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:51.920
you create something that is not received
well, when you don’t win the approval of

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.980
certain people that you maybe want to work
with or have access to or get to “the next

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.410
level.”

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:07.819
But fundamentally I think what it teaches
you that discipline of introspection is one

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:15.310
where you become more fulfilled and happy
because of what you are actually doing that

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:22.470
is true to yourself as opposed to trying to
worry about what others outside expect of

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.470
you.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:29.700
You have to start with your own internal expectations
and those things may evolve but they can only

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.800
evolve because of you.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.670
Not because of someone else giving you an
opportunity or not or someone else approving

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.260
of you or not.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.310
Ultimately at the end of the day how you feel
about yourself is the person that is up in

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.000
here and what’s in here.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:50.670
And that personal commitment was the one that
I found in my journey to go through Hollywood

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.570
which is who is really…who am I?

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:59.780
Who am I truly inside and what do I really
believe about this world looking at things

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:06.660
with new eyes, being critical of myself, not
to the point where you put yourself down (I

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:12.050
think that’s an external issue) but really
one where you go Okay, what do I want to do

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.480
with my life?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.820
What are the things that I believe about this
world?

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.930
Do I believe in the bad things about the world?

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:24.650
Do I also believe in the beauty of the world
and what holds it all together and how am

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:36.370
I going to grow up and how do I affect (through
art) what I see and know to be true and give

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:48.080
something to that that inspires how I feel
in me to others and so it comes from a personal

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:53.639
place where we all have journeys as artists,
we’re sensitive, we’re very open people

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:59.849
but I guess you could say that if you’re
going to use that sensitivity to tell stories

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:02.270
or say things, do it truthfully.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:08.419
Do it through the vehicle of art and your
personal commitment is one that is an evolution

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:09.800
in yourself.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:15.550
So what I knew ten years ago and what I know
today is very different but that doesn’t

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:19.990
mean that what I knew ten years ago was wrong
it’s just all I was able to do at the time

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:22.119
(what I was capable of).

00:05:22.119 --> 00:05:27.169
And so drawing from those experiences, those
hardships, even the times where you feel really

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:35.319
down, you know maybe even depressed in some
cases, is not always at the time that you

00:05:35.319 --> 00:05:40.219
see that as a real opportunity but it is in
those moments that you’re challenged the

00:05:40.219 --> 00:05:45.280
most that shows you not only what you’re
capable of but what you’re also really good

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.949
at because you don’t have everything going
for you the way you expected it to or hoped

00:05:50.949 --> 00:06:00.149
to or wanted it to and so you have to dig
deeper but if your digging deep is to blame

00:06:00.149 --> 00:06:06.779
or attack or get frustrated and say these
people over here are causing me to…they

00:06:06.779 --> 00:06:09.740
don’t know you.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:14.999
They can do whatever they want to do but it’s
about yourself and the journey through that

00:06:14.999 --> 00:06:21.139
process of booming your truest self is the
one that gives you the greatest success (at

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:26.639
least I believe that) because looking back
between where I started on ONE HOUR FANTASY

00:06:26.639 --> 00:06:33.249
GIRL to now with a CHILD’S VOICE and six
movies later in ten years, I am so grateful

00:06:33.249 --> 00:06:40.860
for that process because it had its ups and
downs and the only way that I can measure

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:46.639
it is that I’m happier than I ever have
been in my entire life and I want to keep

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:53.159
getting happier and I want to keep doing stories
that are not talked about.

00:06:53.159 --> 00:06:58.800
I want to do things that help inspire the
good in people because it inspires the good

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.129
in me.

00:07:00.129 --> 00:07:09.249
So the truest part of those statements about
people who…that it [Living in Hollywood]

00:07:09.249 --> 00:07:15.590
doesn’t change you it’s really that you
do fulfill more of who you are if you allow

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:24.210
yourself to commit to that rather than trying
to chase after things and make it so that

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.949
somebody in Hollywood will “pay attention”
to your work.

00:07:26.949 --> 00:07:32.649
But really go out there for the reason that
you want to touch audiences, you want to touch

00:07:32.649 --> 00:07:33.699
people.

00:07:33.699 --> 00:07:36.770
I also said something years ago that I didn’t
really understand at the time.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:40.840
I think it was more of the digital world that
we were emerging in ten years ago after the

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:44.289
financial crash and how everything was going
digital and online.

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:46.940
Obviously it has played itself out quite well.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:53.800
It’s still evolving but I said something
that Hollywood is not the audience, it never

00:07:53.800 --> 00:08:01.759
has been and I would say that irregardless
of what Hollywood does as an industry in its

00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:05.990
executives and all of those things I think
there really great people working in there.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:10.031
And I have no doubt that there are people
who really want to make a different and do

00:08:10.031 --> 00:08:12.270
good things in their work.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:21.929
But at the same time, chasing after those
agendas and and modeling yourself after them

00:08:21.929 --> 00:08:29.149
I think really in art you can become bold
and unique and different and stand out and

00:08:29.149 --> 00:08:34.530
the only way I see people doing that is buy
commitment, full commitment to the belief

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:41.789
in what they’re doing such the point that
it’s not an issue for them about who’s

00:08:41.789 --> 00:08:42.970
getting involved and not.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:48.370
They’re determined to make the film at whatever
level they have to do it with the capacity

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:54.590
and the capabilities…they’re not waiting
on someone else to come in there and just

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:55.590
say “It’s okay.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.730
We’ve got you.”

00:08:56.730 --> 00:09:03.110
It’s really more so what’s up in here
and in here and trying to create that vision

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:08.280
and align people who feel the same way you
do and are joining you on this journey and

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:12.200
going through it because there is a commitment
from within them.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:18.510
I think as a producer there is a responsibility
there to set that kind of tone which is not

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:19.880
an authoritarian one.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:24.410
It’s one of your own self and attracting
those kind of people and that’s how we’ve

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:29.390
been able to do the movies that we’ve done
because we didn’t have big funders.

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.430
We did crowdsourced.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.080
We did our own personal funds.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.530
We brought other people into the mix that
were kind fo like silent investors.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.260
They just wanted us to do well.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:42.330
And I can’t wait for what we do next.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:43.010
I really can’t.

